BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:89c4b95fbf19948c0aebbaf5
SUMMARY:Mutual Dance Theatre presents South Chicago Dance Theatre
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261002T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:South Chicago Dance Theatre October 2-3\, 2026 PRICES Starting 
	at $39. $5 Early Bird Discount for tickets purchased by September 6. Senio
	rs/Students discounts available with valid ID at box office at 650 Walnut 
	St. Mutual Dance Theatre and the Jefferson James Contemporary Dance Theate
	r Series present South Chicago Dance Theatre "THE NEXT BIG THING" — Chicag
	o Tribune Rigor and vulnerability\, side by side The highly buzzed-about S
	outh Chicago Dance Theatre makes its Cincinnati debut\, presented by Mutua
	l Dance Theatre's Jefferson James Contemporary Dance Theater Series! Led b
	y Artistic Director Kia S. Smith\, whose rise has been described as "meteo
	ric\," South Chicago Dance Theatre landed a spot on Dance Magazine's natio
	nal "must-see" list and has been called “the next big thing” by the Chicag
	o Tribune. Described as a "rare combination of rigor and vulnerability" (T
	hird Cost Review)\, South Chicago Dance Theatre blends legacy with innovat
	ion and is the largest company in Mutual's 26-27 season. This program incl
	udes a short excerpt from Smith's Josephine Project\, which traces her gre
	at-grandmother's journey north out of the Jim Crow South\, documented by h
	and-written notes in a preserved suitcase used during the Great Migration.
	 The Josephine Project is only one of five works in the concert. The prese
	ntation features another of Smith's choreographies called Suite on the Sah
	ara\, as well as works by a multi-cultural slate of guest choreographers: 
	On a Lark by Stephanie Martinez\, Slip Force by Natasha Adorlee\, and Subj
	ect(s) Verb Object! by David Dorfman. For more information\, visit mutuald
	ance.org/southchicago. ADDITIONAL EVENTS: Friday\, October 2\, 2026: Post-
	show Q&A. Saturday\, October 3\, 2026\, 12-1:30pm: Off-site masterclass wi
	th South Chicago Dance Theatre's Artistic Director\, Kia S. Smith. Saturda
	y\, October 3\, 2026\, 7pm: Pre-show interview with South Chicago Dance Th
	eatre's Artistic Director\, Kia S. Smith\, hosted by Mutual Dance Theatre'
	s Jeanne Mam-Luft. Saturday\, October\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/ev
	ents/detail/mutual-dance-theatre-presents-south-chicago-dance-theatre
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/mutual-dance-theatre-prese
	nts-south-chicago-dance-theatre
LOCATION:Jarson-Kaplan Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Dance
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
