BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9a0456797c2de749504afb23
SUMMARY:CPI - An Evening of One Act Plays
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261118T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Two One-Act Plays in One Evening! Who Gets Grandma’s Eyeball: A
	 One-Act Play by Paul Bergman Synopsis: Fun and the unexpected connect wit
	h a lucky\, lurking eyeball and Grandma’s estate riddle in this one-act pl
	ay. After the colorful Grandma Maissey dies\, how will the rest figure out
	 the mystery? And where does the funky eyeball land? The challenges and di
	sputes are met with ‘a wink and a prayer’ ...and\, always\, a heartfelt se
	nse of care. Playwright Bio: A retired professional\, Paul enjoys writing 
	stories — both meaningful and fun filled. This play represents the first t
	ime he has engaged with his son\, Alan\, and wife\, Barb\, in creating a s
	cript. They were able to help him find some clever\, off-kilter instances 
	with the characters in this heartwarming show. He dedicates this show to t
	he ‘Bergman Team” and writers everywhere. Waiting Room Commerce: A One-Act
	 Play by Jon Singer Synopsis: Two patients in different stages of knee rep
	lacement surgery engage in conversation while awaiting access to the treat
	ment room. In the holding area\, they engage in the friendly banter of spo
	rts\, kindred lines\, and commonality of spirit. By the time they are call
	ed to physician interaction\, they are thrust into the commerce of anger a
	nd distrust. Playwright Bio: Jonathan (Jon) Singer\, M.D. is a Professor E
	meritus of the Wright State University School of Medicine. He has publishe
	d widely in scientific realms\, including 100 poems in Emergency Medicine 
	periodicals. He authored an autobiography as well as anthologies of non-me
	dical poetry and of short stories. He contributed 50 children's books to p
	rint and electronic media. Three of his plays have had staged readings at 
	the Aronoff.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-an-evenin
	g-of-one-act-plays
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-an-evening-of-one-act-
	plays
LOCATION:Fifth Third Bank Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9e8cc66330853af02800175c
SUMMARY:The Rock Orchestra by Candlelight
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261119T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:After mesmerizing audiences across Europe and the UK\, The Rock
	 Orchestra by Candlelight is set to electrify the USA once again. Prepare 
	for a spellbinding spectacle that infuses iconic rock and metal anthems wi
	th a hauntingly beautiful energy. In an ethereal candlelit setting\, this 
	band of fourteen classical musicians unleashes effortlessly enchanting mel
	odies alongside powerful walls of distortion. Witness the unexpected union
	 of classical music and metal. The UK-based ensemble is a rotating collect
	ive of some of the world’s most talented musicians and vocalists who reima
	gine the music of beloved rock bands\, including Metallica\, AC/DC\, Rolli
	ng Stones\, Rage Against the Machine\, My Chemical Romance\, Linkin' Park\
	, System of a Down\, Guns N' Roses\, Evanescence\, Papa Roach\, The Cranbe
	rries\, and more!\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/the-rock
	-orchestra-by-candlelight
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/the-rock-orchestra-by-cand
	lelight
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Concerts
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ea8893a85e8248a6c6be991a
SUMMARY:2026-27 CMT Mainstage Series
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261122T003000Z
DTEND:20261122T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:The SpongeBob Musical November 13 - 21\, 2026 Based on the Nick
	elodeon animated television series SpongeBob SquarePants\, The SpongeBob M
	usical follows SpongeBob SquarePants’ attempts to avert a volcanic eruptio
	n that could potentially wipe out all life in Bikini Bottom. The musical h
	as been called a "ginormous giggle of a show" that provides a good amount 
	of "giddy\, goofy fun" for all audiences. School of Rock May 7 - 15\, 2027
	 Andrew Lloyd Webber’s award-winning smash hit musical School of Rock is b
	ased on the hilarious hit movie. It follows Dewey Finn\, a failed\, wannab
	e rock star who decides to earn a few extra bucks by posing as a substitut
	e teacher at a prestigious prep school. There he turns a class of straight
	-A students into a guitar-shredding\, bass-slapping\, mind-blowing rock ba
	nd – sensationally performed live by the production’s young actors every n
	ight with roof-raising energy!\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/de
	tail/cmt-mainstage-27
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cmt-mainstage-27
LOCATION:Jarson-Kaplan Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ad44cb8d291c5b49792a5f84
SUMMARY:An Evening with David Sedaris
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261122T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:David Sedaris\, America’s best-selling humorist and social sati
	rist\, returns following publication of his most recent book of short stor
	ies\, Happy Go Lucky\, and his first ever children’s book\, Pretty Ugly. I
	n his customary satirical and humorous manner\, David will make you laugh 
	and think in equal measures\, with all-new\, unpublished stories and comme
	ntary. As always\, the reading will be accompanied by a post-show book sig
	ning.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/david-sedaris-26
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/david-sedaris-26
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Other
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acd134a8a709f1da2b1b8e7d
SUMMARY:O Christmas Tea: A British Comedy 
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261129T003000Z
DTEND:20261129T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Fans of Monty Python\, Mr. Bean\, and Dr. Seuss… Grab your teac
	ups! Combining British propriety with an unabashed love for the unexpected
	\, London’s three-time Impresario Award-winning duo steep an outrageously 
	funny and brilliantly inventive show reminiscent of classic British pantos
	. Rich in wordplay\, comic physicality\, and cleverly crafted interactive 
	elements\, O Christmas Tea is uproarious fun\, yet it is the duo’s boundle
	ss imagination and endearing chemistry that provide the real magic and hea
	rt of this play. When catastrophe strikes at James and Jamesy’s Christmas 
	tea party\, flooding the world with tea\, the duo conjure wildly funny sol
	utions to stay afloat\, and sweep the audience out to sea in a jolly aquat
	ic escapade brimming with whimsy\, action\, and ingenuity in a celebration
	 of friendship at Christmas. “Complete and utter fun… for all ages.” ★★★★★
	 CBC “Outrageously funny\, magnificently written\, beautifully choreograph
	ed.” ★★★★★ London Free Press “An ode to the idea that anything is possible
	.” ★★★★★ Torontoist “I cannot think of a show that will leave you more pro
	foundly happy than this.” ★★★★★ Stage Door Hailed as “a child’s imaginatio
	n on steroids” by London Free Press and “a masterpiece of physical comedy”
	 by Theatre In London\, critics rave for the charismatic James & Jamesy. A
	 must-see performance on the international comedy circuit since 2015\, thi
	s unstoppable duo is regarded as “one of the most popular fringe duos ever
	” (CBC). If the cost is beyond your means\, we invite you to select the Su
	bsidized Ticket option Can't make it on November 28-29? Nov 24: Muncie\, I
	N Dec 19: Dayton\, OH Visit OChristmasTea.com for the full 60-city tour!\n
	\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/o-christmas-tea-a-british-c
	omedy
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/o-christmas-tea-a-british-
	comedy
LOCATION:Jarson-Kaplan Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Comedy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:59a9e4dae4305157455d5b92
SUMMARY:'Twas The Night Before...
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261203T003000Z
DTEND:20261213T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:Cirque du Soleil's holiday-themed family theatrical spectacle a
	rrives in Cincinnati this December. ‘Twas the Night Before... is an exhila
	rating new spin on the beloved Christmas classic as only Cirque du Soleil 
	can imagine. This vibrant acrobatic spectacle about the joy of sharing and
	 friendship promises to spark lasting memories in the hearts of children a
	nd adults alike.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/twas-the-
	night-before
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/twas-the-night-before
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:86228ae0200442b8aee97dce
SUMMARY:David Choate's Hot Chocolate 2026
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20261205T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:The holiday tradition Cincinnati has embraced is back! Now in i
	ts 6th spectacular year\, David Choate's Hot Chocolate: An African America
	n Nutcracker returns to the Aronoff Center\, and rumor has it this year is
	 "hotter" than ever! Hot Chocolate is a fresh production filled with breat
	htaking dance\, unforgettable music\, dazzling visuals\, and the warmth of
	 family\, culture\, and community. Inspired by the timeless magic of The N
	utcracker\, Hot Chocolate reimagines the classic through the richness of t
	he African American experience\, blending ballet with contemporary\, jazz\
