BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9e76fe3f715dfb8c88ba9fcd
SUMMARY:SIX
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270106T003000Z
DTEND:20270110T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:On sale dates are tentative and subject to change. From Tudor Q
	ueens to Pop Icons\, the SIX wives of Henry VIII take the microphone to re
	mix five hundred years of historical heartbreak into a Euphoric Celebratio
	n of 21st century girl power! This new original musical is the global sens
	ation that everyone is losing their head over! The New York Times says SIX
	 “TOTALLY RULES!” (Critic's Pick) and The Washington Post hails SIX as “Ex
	actly the kind of energizing\, inspirational illumination this town aches 
	for!"\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/six-27
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/six-27
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:06afd2d816a2b21770a22175
SUMMARY:ELVIS TRIBUTE ARTIST SPECTACULAR
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270117T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:THE ELVIS TRIBUTE ARTIST SPECTACULAR is an era-by-era tribute c
	oncert celebrating the music and magic of Elvis Presley. The concert begin
	s with the early rockabilly years\, the military years\, the movie years\,
	 the ’68 comeback special in black leather\, and closes with the Las Vegas
	 concert years. The event stars the following acclaimed Elvis Tribute Arti
	sts: SHAWN KLUSH: Shawn was named the first-ever Ultimate Elvis Tribute Ar
	tist by Elvis Presley Enterprises and was named the World’s Greatest Elvis
	 by BBC1 in London. Shawn brings all the electrifying magic of Elvis to th
	e stage. Shawn was named a "Worldwide Ambassador of Elvis" and is “The Clo
	sest Thing to The King in Concert” in Las Vegas. RYAN PELTON: Back by popu
	lar demand\, Ryan is an international award-winning Elvis tribute artist a
	nd actor. Ryan played Blake Rayne in the movie The Identical\, starring As
	hley Judd\, Ray Liotta\, and Seth Green. Ryan continues to entertain audie
	nces all over the world from casinos and theaters to festivals and sports 
	matches. BILL CHERRY: New to this tour\, but certainly not to performing a
	s The King\, Bill was named the Ultimate Elvis Tribute Artist from Elvis P
	resley Enterprises in 2009. EMILIO SANTORO: Direct from the UK\, Emilio wa
	s named the Ultimate Elvis Tribute Artist from Elvis Presley Enterprises i
	n 2024. SPECIAL GUESTS: The Stamps Quartet - the Grammy and Dove award-win
	ning gospel group\, featuring the legendary Ed Enoch\, and members of the 
	Gospel Music Hall of Fame. The Elvis Tribute Artist Spectacular is backed 
	by The Fabulous Ambassadors and The Nashville Dreams.\n\nhttps://www.cinci
	nnatiarts.org/events/detail/elvis-tribute-artist-spectacular-2
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/elvis-tribute-artist-spect
	acular-2
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Concerts
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:27d1c152b73b45ce99aef2aa
SUMMARY:Maybe Happy Ending
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270120T003000Z
DTEND:20270131T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:On sale dates are tentative and subject to change. Winner of 6 
	Tony Awards®\, including Best Musical\, Maybe Happy Ending tells the deepl
	y human story of a chance encounter that sparks connection\, adventure\, a
	nd maybe even love. Helmed by Tony Award-winning director Michael Arden (P
	arade)\, Maybe Happy Ending has been called “one of the best musicals in y
	ears” (USA Today) and even “The best musical in eons!” (Observer). Don’t m
	iss the totally original new musical adventure that explores what it means
	 to be human. Even if they’re not.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/event
	s/detail/maybe-happy-ending
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/maybe-happy-ending
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c0cca8185203aba80c87c14f
SUMMARY:In Harmony 
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270130T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:In Harmony is a musical journey where life and song blend seaml
	essly. This Studio Series event celebrates musical theatre favorites from 
	every era\, chosen to highlight how harmony is something we create togethe
	r. After all\, true harmony only emerges when voices unite. In Life. In So
	ng. In Harmony. Experience the beauty of making music—and life—together.\n
	\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cmt-in-harmony
