BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2b9d8d92050c2646b0e03511
SUMMARY:CPI - Arc of Luminescence
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270330T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Arc of Luminescence: A Full-Length Play by Michael Defrancesco 
	Synopsis: An artist/painter dies. His European collector\, executor\, and 
	live-in meet in NYC. The live-in reveals a private notebook in a locked de
	sk the painter has shared with no one. Its contents unleash a cascade of m
	oral challenges and destructive events. Playwright Bio: Michael Defrancesc
	o graduated with degrees in English and Theater Arts\, and afterwards\, he
	 taught high school for a few years. He fell into work with those living w
	ith developmental disabilities and later founded a residential housing pro
	gram for the developmentally disabled population. After attending a summer
	 drama program at the University of Cincinnati\, Michael was awarded a Roc
	kefeller Grant to UC’s Theatre Arts program\, where he earned a Master’s d
	egree. He began writing plays several years ago\, and Arc of Luminescence 
	is his fifth play selected for a reading with CPI. Michael has previously 
	had CPI staged readings of his plays The Circle\, The Car Ride\, The Hound
	\, and Thump.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-arc-of-l
	uminescence
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-arc-of-luminescence
LOCATION:Fifth Third Bank Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8178af809beeb3e3d99caeaf
SUMMARY:Director’s Vision: Two Voices
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270402T233000Z
DTEND:20270404T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Performance Times April 2\, 2027 7:30PM April 3\, 2027 2:00PM A
	pril 3\, 2027 7:30PM April 4\, 2027 1:00PM Director’s Vision: Two Voices i
	nvites audiences to experience two distinct artistic perspectives that spe
	ak to who we are and how we connect. This double bill features acclaimed S
	outh African choreographer Mthuthuzeli November\, who challenges our dance
	rs to explore movement as a catalyst of change through unity. Complementin
	g this contemporary work is George Balanchine’s Square Dance\, which gives
	 voice to the American spirit by fusing folk traditions with the clarity a
	nd precision of classical ballet. Though these works emerge from different
	 artistic paths\, they converge in a shared expression of humanity\, invit
	ing audiences to experience two voices that ultimately leave as one. Info 
	& Ordering Cincinnati Ballet Box Office 513-621-5282 1801 Gilbert Avenue |
	 Cincinnati\, OH 45202 Additional Info and Hours\n\nhttps://www.cincinnati
	arts.org/events/detail/ballet-directors-vision-27
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/ballet-directors-vision-27
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Dance
END:VEVENT
