BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:09f6125c3f05ddfdfa7e9a65
SUMMARY:Harry Potter and the Cursed Child 
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270414T233000Z
DTEND:20270425T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:On sale dates are tentative and subject to change. IT’S TIME TO
	 BELIEVE IN MAGIC Broadway’s spellbinding spectacular Harry Potter and the
	 Cursed Child is coming to Cincinnati. Join the next adventure and experie
	nce the wizarding world like never before at this record-breaking hit and 
	winner of six Tony Awards® including Best Play. “It’s one of the most defi
	ning pop culture events of the decade” (Forbes). When Harry Potter’s head-
	strong son Albus befriends the son of his fiercest rival\, Draco Malfoy\, 
	it sparks an unbelievable new journey for them all—with the power to chang
	e the past and future forever. Prepare for a mind-blowing race through tim
	e\, spectacular spells\, and an epic battle\, all brought to life with the
	 most astonishing theatrical magic ever seen on stage. It’s a “marvel of i
	magination” (The New York Times) that will “leave you wondering ‘how’d the
	y do that?’ for days to come” (People Magazine).\n\nhttps://www.cincinnati
	arts.org/events/detail/harry-potter-and-the-cursed-child
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/harry-potter-and-the-curse
	d-child
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d8d503db500b88a6fcc7eccd
SUMMARY:CPI - Behind the Scene  
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270427T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Behind the Scene: A Full-Length Comedy by Susan & Doug Decatur 
	Synopsis: In 1933\, the movie industry is about to enact new censorship st
	andards. Young Helen\, who dreams of becoming a movie star\, runs a lodge 
	with her boyfriend\, George. When a Hollywood film crew checks in to shoot
	 their first “talkie” on location before these movie restrictions take eff
	ect\, things go right and wrong in the midst of everyone involved seeking 
	hope\, love\, and redemption. Playwright Bios: Susan and Doug became a wri
	ting team after their marriage in 2018. They’ve co-written three full-leng
	th plays\, including Unfinished Business\, a 2020 Austin Film Festival sec
	ond round selection and Screencraft Finalist\, in addition to Martha’s Wil
	l\, which was also an Austin Film Festival second round selection in 2025.
	 They also collaborated on Lovestruck\, a compilation of eight 10-minute p
	lays inspired by their own love story. All three plays were performed at t
	he Aronoff Center. Behind the Scene is their fourth CPI staged play togeth
	er. The Decaturs are also National Senior Games athletes. Doug won a Gold 
	Medal in Basketball and Susan won a Silver Medal in the 50-Meter Track and
	 Field event. They also enjoy playing tennis\, ballroom dancing\, hiking\,
	 and eating dark chocolate.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detai
	l/cpi-behind-the-scene
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-behind-the-scene
LOCATION:Fifth Third Bank Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0539946c0277ca0eb986a549
SUMMARY:Mutual Dance Theatre in Modern Mix '27
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20270430T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Mutual Dance Theatre in MODERN MIX '27 PRICES: Starting at $29.
	 $5 Early Bird Discount for tickets purchased by April 4\, 2027. Seniors/S
	tudents discounts available with valid ID at box office at 650 Walnut St. 
	This tour de force is Cincinnati's best-kept secret Modern Mix closes Mutu
	al Dance Theatre's 55th anniversary season on the Aronoff Center's Jarson-
	Kaplan Theater mainstage: four very different choreographers\, four choreo
	graphies\, one tour de force of dance. Modern Mix is an annual series that
	 connects our immensely talented resident company with national guests and
	 our own resident creations. Each attention-demanding iteration creates su
	rprising juxtapositions and rising popularity. This 2027 program reprises 
	two seminal works created in-house: Steven P. Evans\, a former Mutual Danc
	e Theatre company director\, returns with Petrichor (2023). Named for the 
	scent of rain after a long dry spell\, dancers move beneath relief made vi
	sible: an ascending and descending canopy of lightbulbs. Artistic Director
	 Jeanne Mam-Luft's /SHIFT/ (2014) is a beloved\, powerful work depicting a
	 society after a catastrophic event that led to changes in power. /SHIFT/ 
	holds the Mutual Dance Theatre record for juried festivals across the coun
	try and returns to the stage where it began. Hana Delong's choreographic c
	hops were first noticed by Mutual Dance Theatre director Jeanne Mam-Luft w
	hen presented here in 2023. A member of Dallas Black Dance Theatre for man
	y years and a furniture maker (!)\, Delong trained at the Ailey School and
	 has performed in works by such greats as Martha Graham\, Doug Varone\, Ma
	tthew Rushing\, Alvin Ailey\, Hope Boykin\, and many others\, gracing the 
	stages of Jacob's Pillow\, Lincoln Center\, and The Joyce. Rodrigo Almaral
	es makes his Mutual Dance Theatre premiere with a new commission. A former
	 dancer with Cincinnati Ballet\, Almarales was born into ballet: both of h
	is parents were principal dancers with Cuba's National Ballet. Almarales t
	rained at Cuba's National Scho\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/de
	tail/mutual-dance-theatre-in-modern-mix-27
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/mutual-dance-theatre-in-mo
	dern-mix-27
LOCATION:Jarson-Kaplan Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Dance
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
